WEBVTT

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:04.900
I'm Taniyama Mai,

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.560
1st-Year high-schooler.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.230
At last, the exorcism
at the old schoolhouse had begun.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.240
First, Priestess did her exorcism,
but it failed spectacularly!

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.570
She even got the principal injured!

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:20.200
After that, many strange
occurrences followed.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.250
Monk says that the spirits were getting
violent after the failed exorcism,

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.250
and he may be right.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.800
And yet, Naru says that this
is all due to the ground sinking.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.300
I'm so mad at myself,
I could throw up.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:37.600
But after Naru went off somewhere,
Monk did his exorcism,

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.930
but the poltergeist phenomena
just got more intense!

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.060
It's so warm...

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:46.270
Objects that poltergeists
move feel warm to the touch.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.270
Little Lady!

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.380
Naru...

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.720
You're back, are you? Good...

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.260
Um, listen, there really does
seem to be a poltergeist!

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.390
Urgh- ow...

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.940
You should rest a little longer.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.070
What's come over you?
You're being so nice, Naru...

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:59.400
You should always smile like that...

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.410
Hey, Little Lady!

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.740
She's coming around.

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.410
Hey, are you all right?

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.830
We thought you were dead!

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:14.840
Sorry...

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.750
You were out for a good while.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:18.420
It's already 4 o'clock
in the morning.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.090
Did Naru come back?

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:21.590
Nope.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.430
Oh. Then it was a dream.
I guess it would have to be.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:30.100
There's no way Naru
would smile like that.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.100
Where's Kuroda-san?

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.310
She went home.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.110
Say, don't you think something
feels wrong here?

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.440
The exorcisms had
absolutely no effect.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.820
It's about time we thought
about our own safety, isn't it?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.780
You're saying you want to run away?

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.120
Now, look! It was your boss
who ran away first, wasn't it!?

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.120
He's probably at home,
quivering right now!

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.790
Are you serious about this?

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.120
No, he probably ran away
because of us.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.290
We did all gang up on him
this afternoon, after all.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.130
You mean, that incredibly
swollen-headed, self-assured,

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:01.470
world's-greatest
holier-than-thou narcissist?

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.140
In Shibuya-san's case,
he probably got mad and went home

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.800
to make up some straw effigy dolls,
don't you think?

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:18.820
Good morning.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.570
Good morning!

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:24.030
Hey, Mai, I heard you had something
terrible happen yesterday.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.490
Huh? How do you know?

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:31.160
From Kuroda-san. She's been
bragging about it to everyone.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.290
Still, it was surprising, huh?

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:38.000
Mm-hmm, out of nowhere,
Shibuya-san called us up.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:38.840
When!?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.510
Last night, right?

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:41.170
Uh-huh.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:44.510
Last night? He's been
missing since yesterday!

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:45.840
What did you talk about?

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:51.180
U-um... this and that. Stuff about
the old schoolhouse, as well as, um...

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:53.520
As well as stuff about Kuroda-san.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.850
What is that guy up to!?

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.190
Oh, there you are.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:58.980
Kuroda...

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.070
Taniyama...

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.360
Come to the Principal's Office.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.700
Excuse us.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.280
Naru?

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:12.620
Masako... and everyone else? Why?

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.540
Sit down.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.210
This is now everyone who is involved
with this case, right?

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.550
All right, let me have
a little of your time.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.560
That's a strange light.
It comes on, then goes back off.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.060
Please focus on the light.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.900
Please match your breathing
to the light.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:52.910
Slowly now... relax your shoulders...

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.590
Can you hear yourself breathing?

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:03.250
I feel sort of sleepy...

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.920
Maybe it's because of what
happened last night...

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.590
I could just be tired...

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:13.260
Inside your mind,
please count your breaths.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.600
Naru's voice is so far away...

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:21.270
Tonight, the chair on the 2nd floor
of the old schoolhouse will move.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:22.940
Chair?

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:26.940
Tonight, in the laboratory,
in the old schoolhouse.

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:31.780
Laboratory... chair... chair...

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.950
Very good. Thank you very much.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.290
That sure is bright.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.210
What's going on here?

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:44.630
The chair...

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.960
Naru!

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.970
Where did you go yesterday?

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:51.970
Here and there. I heard you got hurt.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:55.640
It wasn't any big deal.
Say, what was that earlier?

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.310
Don't you have to get back to class?

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.890
Never mind that.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:02.020
I get it. You want to be stupid.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.650
Hold on, there's something
I wanted to ask you.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.650
Did you come back last night?

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.320
To the old schoolhouse? No. Why?

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:13.870
Oh, um, no reason.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:17.160
Well, I'm going back
to my classroom. Bye-bye.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:24.670
Yeah, right. No way would
Naru smile like that.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.840
Mm-mm, it was a dream.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:34.010
So, why was I... Does that mean...
does that mean...

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:50.360
Ah, no! I'm remembering it,
no matter what I do!

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:52.530
Then, I really am...

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.370
D-don't look over here!

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.710
Mai, were you the one who set up the
microphone on the 2nd floor last night?

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:05.380
Uh-huh. The video end came out fine,
but I wasn't sure if...

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.550
It was a pretty good job, for you.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.800
It picked up some
fairly interesting sound.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:15.300
What?

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:19.720
Huh? Oh, nothing.
Hey, you know those shoe cubbies?

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:23.390
The ones that fell over?
They were warm! You said that objects

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:27.060
that poltergeists moved had
elevated temperatures, right?

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.730
I'm impressed you remembered.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:29.730
Mm-hmm.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.400
Oh, Mai-san's here, too.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.070
John?

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:35.870
All right, shall we get started?

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:43.410
A chair, and a night-vision camera?

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:47.590
Hey... Hey, I said!
Naru-chan, what's that?

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.090
Radar.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.920
You mean, that thing that's
on airplanes and stuff?

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.090
What are you using it for?

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:55.430
If I told you, it wouldn't work.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.430
But I'm your assistant.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:00.100
Take that plywood over there,

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.270
and board up all the windows
and doors in this room for me.

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:09.940
For crying out loud, he could at least
tell me a little bit, couldn't he!?

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.790
All finished...

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.130
Both of you, sign all of the boards.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:35.680
We're finished writing...

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:39.800
All right, then sign here, too.
When you finish, you can go home.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:42.680
Say, what's the meaning of all this?

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.600
You'll find out, come tomorrow.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.480
Hold on, Naru!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.650
Shibuya-san has
something in mind.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.820
Why don't we just
wait until tomorrow?

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:56.490
Tomorrow, then!
Tomorrow, tomorrow, tomorrow!

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.660
...or so I thought,

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.660
but it's bothering me so much,
I couldn't sleep at all!

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.250
It's the real assistant.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.670
This is so awkward. I'm the one
who got him hurt, and all...

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.840
You're awfully early, aren't you?

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:23.180
W-well, I can't stop thinking about
that thing we set up yesterday.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.180
Wait a little while longer.
Everyone will be here soon.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:28.600
Everyone? You mean,
Priestess, and those guys?

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:29.900
But why?

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.860
W-what's with him!?

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.360
A-are you feeling better now?

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.860
Hurry up and get here, everyone!

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.540
So then, what are you going
to show us today?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.500
Shouldn't you give it up now,
before you embarrass yourself?

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:53.210
Mai, John, confirm that the paper you
signed yesterday hasn't been torn.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.550
Let's see...

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.670
It looks fine, the same as yesterday.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.880
Yes.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.220
All right...

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:17.900
Shibuya-san...

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.240
Shibuya-san!

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.910
The chair...

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.910
The chair has moved!

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.250
Yes, it has.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.580
H-hang on, what does this mean?

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.580
Hey, Naru-chan!

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.420
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.970
I will be leaving sometime today.

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:43.590
You're not saying that you've
solved the case, are you?

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.260
That's what I'm saying.

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:46.600
The ground sinking?

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:49.930
Yes, I believe that that explains
everything about the case

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.600
that the principal hired me for.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:56.610
Ha! So how do you explain the
disturbance the day before yesterday?

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:58.280
That was poltergeisting.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:59.610
If you know that, then how-

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:01.030
What else could he do?

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.530
He's incapable of driving
the spirits out, right?

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.950
I do not believe
it will be necessary.

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:09.540
Would you like to see?

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:29.970
W-was that?

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.310
That is full-fledged
poltergeisting, isn't it?

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:36.310
Humans are to blame for half
of poltergeist phenomena.

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:39.650
You mean, pranks?
But no one could get in here.

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:42.650
Yes. We sealed off all
of the entrances.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.660
I even had Mai
and John sign everything,

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:47.320
so we would know if someone
had forced their way in.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.330
Even if they tried to replace
any broken boards,

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:52.540
they wouldn't have been able to
perfectly duplicate our signatures.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:55.330
That more than proves that
it was the work of spirits.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:59.000
I placed a suggestion yesterday
with everyone who is here,

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.670
that in the evening,
this chair would move.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.340
In the Principal's Office...

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:07.010
I'm pretty sure- at least as of yet-

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.680
this method has ever failed me.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:13.350
But no one was able
to get into this room.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.850
Poltergeisting is a variety
of supernatural ability.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.690
It's done by people who have
an unconscious craving to be noticed,

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:21.360
and for people to pay attention
to them, when for whatever cause,

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.690
enough stress builds up within them.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:28.700
In such cases, when a suggestion
is planted, it then comes about.

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:32.370
Wants to be paid attention to?
Wants to be noticed?

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.700
You grandstander.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:36.040
You just want make
yourself conspicuous.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.380
She's always been weird.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:44.050
Ever since middle school,
she's been famous for being trouble.

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:49.050
Y-you're saying,
I'm the one who did it?

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:52.390
From the start, I felt like
you were drawing my attention.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:56.730
For example, you said that you
saw spirits here from the war.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:00.400
But there were no stories about this
area being bombed during the war,

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:03.730
or of this school being
used as a hospital,

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:07.150
nor was it true that there was
ever a hospital built here.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:11.740
That would mean that you were either
mistaken, or intentionally lying.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.410
I wasn't lying!

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:16.410
I thought you were just pretending
to be spiritually sensitive at first,

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:20.080
so when phenomena occurred that could
only be considered poltergeisting,

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.750
I was honestly at a loss.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:25.420
This, after my instruments measured
no data, and in Hara-san's judgment,

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.090
I concluded that there
were no spirits here.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:30.430
So the cause had to be human.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:34.430
Poltergeisting is generally caused
by children in their early teens.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:37.100
There are also cases
in spiritually sensitive girls.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:40.440
They do it unconsciously,
when extreme stress builds up.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.770
The underlying currents are...

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:47.440
Please, look at me...
turn towards me...

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:51.530
You were famous for being spiritually
sensitive, ever since middle school.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:54.790
Once it was proven to you that the
evil spirits in the old schoolhouse

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:58.460
could all be blamed on
the land sinking underneath it,

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:01.460
naturally, you'd lose whatever faith
you had in yourself up until then

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.250
in having spiritual abilities.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:07.130
You felt a great pressure from
your intense apprehension,

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:10.130
and unconsciously,
you thought to yourself,

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.970
"no, that can't be.
There have to be spirits here.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.470
They can't not be here.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:18.810
There has to be poltergeisting
going on here. It has to happen."

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.810
And then...

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:24.820
She unconsciously carried it out, huh?

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:27.820
I believe she is a latent psychic.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.150
"Saikikku"?

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:32.490
One who has supernatural abilities.
She may not be aware of it,

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:36.490
but she probably has some level of PK.

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:40.830
I'll just say this for Mai's sake,
but PK stands for psychokinesis.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.920
Well, thank you for being so kind.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:47.840
For Kuroda-san, it was necessary
that there be evil spirits present,

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:50.840
in order for her to keep
garnering attention around her.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:53.430
In order for her to be who she was.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:58.430
I can kind of understand
how that would feel.

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:02.190
Really, everyone wants
to think that they're special.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:05.860
That there's something special about
them, that everyone else recognizes.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.530
It doesn't matter what it is,
they just want some special talent

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:11.530
that sets them apart from others.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:12.860
Kuroda-san, for you,

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:15.530
I'm sure it must have been
your spiritual abilities, huh?

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:24.540
Does that satisfy everyone?

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:28.880
Not yet. By that explanation,
her elevated stress came about

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:31.880
after you gave your theory
about the ground sinking, right?

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:34.220
Then, what about me being
shut up inside that classroom,

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:36.550
and the video being erased?

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:41.230
Priestess, in your case, it's because
this was stuck into the door's groove.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:42.890
A nail?

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:46.360
Open up! Hey, open the door!

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:51.440
I noticed it right away, but I
didn't think it was worth mentioning.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:55.240
You mean, someone did it on purpose!?

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:56.370
It was you, huh!?

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.580
You just meant it as
a little prank, right?

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:03.580
Just before, Priestess appeared
to have words with you, and all.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:04.920
Then, what about the video?

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:07.580
That was intentionally erased.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:12.590
Priestess, when you got shut in,
we all left the base.

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:16.930
There was plenty of time to manipulate
it when no one would see.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.260
Do you believe this girl?

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.270
So, what do we do?

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:25.270
The principal hired us to make
this place ready for construction.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:28.270
I plan to report this
to the principal:

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:32.940
The old schoolhouse was haunted
by those who died in the war.

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:36.280
They have been exorcised, so you
may go ahead with construction.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.950
Is that okay with you, Kuroda-san?

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.950
How very kind of you.

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:48.630
But are you sure you shouldn't
tell him the truth?

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:52.050
She is keeping herself
suppressed enough, even now.

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:55.300
I don't think it's necessary
to run her down any further.

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:58.680
Naru...

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:02.180
Hmm... Naru, you're quite
the feminist, huh?

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:03.640
Got a girlfriend?

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.310
I'm not sure I understand
the point of your question.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.810
I wouldn't mind putting
up with you,

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:10.310
younger though you are.

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:12.650
I appreciate you saying so,

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:14.190
but unfortunately, I can't.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.530
I'm too used to looking
in the mirror.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.990
So, who exactly are we going
to say performed the exorcism!?

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:25.200
Everyone worked together.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.830
Nobody minds that, do they?

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.000
Mai...

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.670
I know.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:37.340
Lin, let's start breaking camp.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.720
Right.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:46.020
It was no big deal, was it?

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:48.190
You were still pretty
anxious, considering.

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:49.350
Cut the kidding.

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:52.360
Everyone's leaving.
I guess they would, too.

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:56.360
The investigation is over,
so there's no reason to stay here.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:58.150
Shouldn't you be going to class?

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:01.030
Oh, I was going to see you off.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:03.700
After all, it may not have been for
very long, but you were my boss.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:07.700
No need. Why don't you
hurry back to class?

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:11.040
If you get any dumber, it will
be beyond anyone's control.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.710
Oh, is that right!? Very well!

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:16.170
I'll work as hard
as I can to smarten up!

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:20.220
Well, goodbye!

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:25.390
It's so stupid, me being the only
one who will miss the other one!

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:30.730
Fine, then! This is it!
I'm going to forget all about you!

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:43.930
Kuroda-san, that's amazing!

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:46.470
So there really were ghosts
in the old schoolhouse!

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:50.140
Plus, it all collapsed
the other day.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:52.810
We're the ones who
should be sighing.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:57.480
Yeah. Mai, why didn't you ask
Shibuya-san for his address and such?

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.690
He's not in the phone book, either.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:04.700
Taniyama Mai-san in room 1-F,
you have a telephone call.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:07.990
Please come to the office.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.490
Hello?

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:11.830
Is that you, Mai?

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.160
Y-yes!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:15.830
You don't have to yell.

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:20.050
That big-shot tone and way
of speaking- it's Naru, all right.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:22.510
W-what are you calling me about?

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:23.840
Your fee.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:24.510
Huh?

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:27.180
Your payment for assisting me.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:29.050
If you don't want it,
that's fine, too.

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:31.850
A business matter!? Geez...

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:35.850
Okay, I'll send it to you within
the week. One more thing-

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:38.980
Does your school allow you
to have a job?

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:41.190
If you'd like, how about
coming to work for me?

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:43.860
It's office work,
but I could use another hand.

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:46.530
Y-yes! I'll do it!

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.570
Okay, come on down sometime.

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:52.540
The location is in
Shibuya-ku, Dogenzaka.

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:56.210
Also, you were a big help earlier.

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.540
Thanks.

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:06.340
And that's how I came to work
at Shibiya Psychic Research-

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:09.140
or SPR for short.

00:23:44.310 --> 00:23:49.320
Next time: File 2,
"The Doll House" #1
